WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Citizens of the city, heed my warning!

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.070
Delzaine, the King of Endora, has betrayed us!

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.040
Our country is on the verge of disaster!

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.950
He knew the Warp Particles, which comprise our world, were dying!

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.120
And yet, he kept secret this truth from the public!

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.760
The king has abandoned Endora and fled from this world.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.430
He has left us like sheep without a shepherd.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:36.070
Soon, the omnipresent Adamas will lose its light and plunge us into darkness!

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.230
What will become of Endora?!

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.040
Is our world coming to an end?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.130
I don't wanna die! Save me!

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:55.910
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:05.920
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:16.310
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:26.300
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:36.480
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:47.000
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:57.000
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.680
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.640
Delzaine was killed by his henchmen?

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.400
Yeah.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.910
It's troubling how much havoc this Ibelda is creating.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.350
I'm sure we'll have to deal with him again in the near future.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.550
But right now, your island takes priority.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.350
How is it?

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.250
Well, the enemy commands five ships.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.320
They still have yet to reach land.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:45.350
I see... Hopefully Ralph and the others can hold it until we arrive.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.700
I deeply appreciate the Ignauts' support.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.570
I hope that my absence doesn't cost us.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:59.870
It's the least we could do for all that you've helped us.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.280
So is Babel not working anymore?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.920
That seems to be the case for now.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.120
Ah, shucks.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.050
I came to tell you what our research revealed about Babel. Have a minute?

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.580
Yes, please.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.730
"16: Longing"

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.130
This is the true form of Babel.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.130
Just seeing that doesn't tell me anything.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.100
What?!

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.070
Explain it in terms I can understand!

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.440
We all know Babel is an ancient device.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:37.110
One that allows transport between Endora and the surface.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.210
Yeah...

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:43.450
The designs I worked on of Babel only dealt with the Endora side.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:48.950
It seems that the exit on the surface is entirely blocked.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:55.500
His design was utterly flawless and we fixed the problematic gauges.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:01.240
But it's impossible to use it for transport even if the particles successfully disassemble.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:05.010
Which might explain why
Ibelda became a monster.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:12.110
Without both the Endora and surface sides open,
Babel will not work as planned.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.780
It's a good thing I didn't go first...

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.450
This discovery also tells us one more thing...

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:18.350
Hmm?

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.190
What is it, Pascal?

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.030
It's regarding the decline of Warp Particles.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.960
Warp Particles? What's that again?

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.930
The energy forming the basis of everything in Endora.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.770
Oh, that.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.200
The thing that lets us use Warp Relics, right?

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.040
Precisely.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:40.040
The truth is, we found data showing the decrease of particles over recent years.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:46.480
Joseph and I had a hypothesis that it was somehow connected to Babel.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:52.050
But now, knowing Babel is closed and unable to transfer particles...

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.990
...means our hypothesis has to be scrapped.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.550
That's not good.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.160
And still the Warp Particles are decreasing?

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.500
Yeah...

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.870
Eljuia's vision might actually come true.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:13.040
The one where the power protecting Endora is lost and our world is destroyed?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.910
World destruction? I see...
Now the message from this morning makes sense.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.050
What's that?

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.920
Word came from an ally at the capital.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.690
Radicals preaching about dwindling
Warp Particles and the end of the world

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:29.360
are inciting panic in the people.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.160
Seriously?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.060
The worse the rumor, the faster it spreads.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.600
It's crippling those in the capital who are fighting for peace.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.870
It's equally hard stopping the rumor as it is finding the truth.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.770
This country is chaotic enough as it is.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.380
People panicking about the end of the world is like throwing fuel onto the fire.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.680
Yet another fire to put out...

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.710
Emilio...

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.580
Let's do it!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.520
We'll put everything we've got into finding out

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.790
why Warp Particles are decreasing and what we can do about it.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.960
Both to find out the truth and to help everyone calm down again.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.390
We sure will.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.430
Don't you worry, Shun.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:12.530
We'll definitely find a way to get you back home.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.770
No, forget about me.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.610
If Endora's in trouble, focus on that first.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.040
It's all right!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.140
Just leave it to Pascal.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.410
That's right.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.710
Don't underestimate the greatest scientist in Endora.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.950
Don't forget about me either.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.280
You're the greatest weirdos in Endora.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.420
Step away for a minute and the problems just pile up.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.260
At least it won't be boring.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.820
But think how much trouble it will be.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.900
U-Um... Could you all please just try to get along?

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:50.110
That was my plan from the start, but Guidoro...

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.270
What was Demetrio thinking?!

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.310
Inviting the leader of the Truculent...

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.310
Didn't we already go through this?

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.150
I only joined with Demetrio to fulfill my one objective.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.420
I don't recall ever needing your permission.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.750
H-Hey! Be careful what you say!

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:08.190
He might not be very polite, but Guidoro isn't a bad person!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:08.960
Says you.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.030
Huh?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.790
You're both enemies.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.030
What?!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.630
I'll just tell Demetrio you fell in the sea.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.340
You're just kidding, right?

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.110
You're like a short-tempered child!

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.840
I'm not a child!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.830
Come on. Bring it.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.290
Guidoro, cut it out!

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.620
Would everyone just calm down already?!

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.500
Enough!

00:07:55.900 --> 00:08:00.310
I ask that you entrust these two to me.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.010
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.180
Gradido! You don't...

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.180
Demetrio!

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:06.150
Yeah?

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.020
I wish to join the Ignauts!

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:15.420
As a fellow inhabitant of Endora, I cannot ignore the peril of the country any longer.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.860
I'm leaving the island to join you!

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.660
I've been waiting for you to say that.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.030
I'm sure.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:24.700
The sins of these two cannot be erased.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:30.770
But there are none who don't regret something they've done in the past.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:34.380
When a Zoozian asks to be entrusted with another's life...

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.780
...it's proof that they're willing to die to protect them!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.720
Will you not put your hatred to rest?

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.790
Why don't you two give it up?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.030
Our Zoozian buddy here gives quite the speech.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.030
Let's all just call it a truce, all right?

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:53.730
Uh...

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.930
So much for that.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.590
You're not my boss. Hmph!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.110
I couldn't have asked for a better ally.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.540
I owe you one.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.640
I promise to be your sword to whatever end.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.820
The enemy's attacking!

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.960
Prepare for battle!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.600
Keep in formation!

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.460
Hold out until daybreak!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.240
They should've just surrendered and been content being my slaves!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:40.230
Fine by me. All who oppose me are as good as dead!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.650
Wh-What?!

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.850
Sorry, but you don't get to decide our fate.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.850
H-How did you get here?!

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:55.020
I'll let you wash your sins in the waves of the sea if you turn and leave now.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:58.960
Hey now, aren't you being a little too generous?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.930
Y-You're full of it!
What can just two of you do?!

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.030
Two is plenty for you folks.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.110
And don't you come back!

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:46.340
We'll head this way for the capital and smother riots as we go.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:50.080
Meanwhile, I'd like for the
Zoozians to stabilize the north.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.180
Sure. We're familiar with those lands, too.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.550
We can move out soon.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.590
Given the situation, it's a tough request, but...

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:02.090
You want us to minimize bloodshed. Isn't that right?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.260
You know me well.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:07.860
That's just the kind of person you are.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:11.770
This guy just joined and he's stealing our thunder...

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.240
Shun, I've been thinking...

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:14.670
Hmm?

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.540
Father! Welcome back!

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.540
Thanks. I'm home.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.540
Did he say father?!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.070
You have a son?

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:25.240
Oh? He looks just like you.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:32.250
Crum, these people are your father's dear comrades.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.720
Say hello to them.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.060
Ah, we made him cry.

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:42.960
Wow, he hates us already.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:46.090
It's because you and Emilio have such scary faces.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:50.310
You're the one with the face of an ass.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.410
What was that?! Try saying it again!

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.440
I said you look stupid.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.410
Shut up, you moping prince.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.880
Stop making a scene you two.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.550
Father!

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:06.990
Hey, hey. If you want to be a strong Zoozian, you can't be such a crybaby.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.750
You're strong like me, aren't you?

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:14.800
So? Is this about what you said earlier?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.270
Yeah. I want to talk to you and Demetrio about something.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.740
Let's hear it.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.840
It's about Gradido going to suppress the north.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.770
I don't think it will go as smooth as you think.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:26.310
Huh?

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.310
And why's that?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:33.680
In this country, most of the people view the Zoozians as savage animals.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:38.850
With all the chaos and unrest, sending Zoozians to bring order is a bad idea.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:42.860
If it's just them by themselves, no one will obey their orders.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:46.490
Even I thought they were savages at first...

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:53.370
It's easy to form a prejudice by appearance and rumors.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.370
You can't blame anyone for being cautious.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:13:02.310
So, I think it's best if you sent some people along to help see things through.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.950
Emilio, you...

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.350
What?

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:11.320
Is this the same guy who said before that Zoozians couldn't be reasoned with?

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.460
Shut up, you moron.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.020
It's true though!

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:15.890
Shut up!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.060
Care if I steal that idea?

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.900
I know a father who wants to make his son proud.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.700
--No. Please do.
--You're choking me! I'm dying!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.140
Ah! This feels so good!

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:34.340
We haven't taken a break like this in forever!

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:37.380
It really cleanses the heart and soul.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.370
It's hard to believe that the world may be coming to an end.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:48.220
If the Warp Particles keep vanishing, will we lose this beautiful scenery, too?

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:53.200
I wonder if there's anything
I can do to help Endora?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.660
Oh? I'm pretty sure there is.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:55.330
Hmm?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.600
Something only you can do.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.900
What is it? Tell me!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.600
It's simple really.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.270
Get married to Emilio and help revive the Royal Family.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.410
What?!

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:10.180
True, that is something only Alicia can do.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.450
What? Why me?!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.920
You didn't think we'd figure you out?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.180
The color of your heart is as obvious as can be.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.460
Th-That's not true!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:26.960
Emilio is my childhood friend!
That's all there is to it!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:32.600
He even ditched me and ran away!
I'm sure Emilio doesn't feel anything for me...

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.100
True. You're more like a mother than anything.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.070
Really?!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.710
Louise...

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.040
Isn't that the truth?

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.410
I don't even know myself.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:48.620
Do I think he's a friend or something else?

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:53.260
Like, thinking how Emilio might get trapped in a Warp Relic...

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.810
It worries me crazy...

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:58.130
Don't you worry.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:01.130
I no longer sense any hatred from him.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.600
Won't you tell him your feelings?

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:09.400
Emilio is too busy now searching for his purpose in the world.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.410
I need to grow up and do the same thing myself.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.670
And if all that happens and Emilio and I are still in it together...

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:22.620
Then that's when I think
I'll tell him my feelings.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.190
I know exactly how you feel!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:25.950
Huh?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.820
It's the same way I feel about Demetrio.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.830
Huh?!

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.530
Don't tell me you've got a thing for Demetrio...

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.030
Another enemy!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:40.800
We stand together as comrades with a joined purpose in the world...

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.800
Isn't that right?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.840
Uh... Comrades, right?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.530
Too ambiguous...

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.970
If you want to be a strong Zoozian, you can't be such a crybaby.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.670
Yo!

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:58.850
I see...

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.520
If Gradido leaves the island, you won't get to see much of him.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.960
No...

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.970
Won't your father be worried that you're gone?

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.670
Don't tell him I cried, okay?

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:17.970
All right.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.580
Is that really what you want?

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:26.550
But... If I can't show him I'm strong, he won't feel right about leaving the island.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.750
You...

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:30.390
You're still just a child.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:34.920
Your father is on a brave mission to save the world.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:39.380
Not because he's the King of the Zoozians, but because he has you.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:45.160
If you're sad, tell him. Tell him how much you love and admire him.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.240
You don't think he'll get angry?

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:52.500
Your father's too cool a guy to do that.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.010
Okay.

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:58.680
Have a good talk with your father.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.080
I will.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.280
What a huge catch!

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:04.520
Dammit...

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:05.790
Crum!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.290
You're late! You had us worried.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.260
Father! I'm sorry!

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.530
Go on.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.230
Father...

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:18.130
Father, good luck with your mission!

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:21.200
Mother and I will take care while you're gone.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:26.140
So... So... Come back healthy and strong!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.280
Spoken well, Crum.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:37.220
Your father will be sure to succeed for the sake of you and your mother.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:40.450
I promise I will not disappoint you.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.940
It's time to call it a night.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.770
We leave early tomorrow.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.140
Sorry...

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.910
I know how you feel.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.680
But rushing isn't going to help.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:03.670
Right.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:07.280
Emilio?

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.620
What brings you here so late?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.820
I need to ask you something.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.090
I'll excuse myself.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.090
No, it's fine if you stay.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:20.300
What did you want to ask Delzaine in Babylon?

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:22.360
You're curious about the king?

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:23.360
Yeah.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.630
I see...

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.870
This is just a conjecture of mine, but...

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:31.810
I believe he wanted to meet somebody on the surface.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:37.350
It was about ten or so years before your real father Alzerm Langheim sat on the throne.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:43.650
His younger brother King Delzaine was entrusted with unifying the northern continent.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:46.320
Back when Babel was still operational?

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:49.990
He was probably the first one to reach it.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:54.200
What did Delzaine see at Babel?!

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.700
I don't know...

00:18:55.700 --> 00:19:00.070
I've looked for documents in the Royal
Laboratory but there are no official records.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:05.240
Do you remember anything from that time, Prince Emilio?

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.810
I... can't even remember my father's face.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:13.480
Emilio would have only been two when King Alzerm passed away.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.720
He wouldn't remember anything.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.720
There's so much that I wish I knew.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:21.660
You'll just have to take it slow and learn.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:26.090
There are plenty of records about
King Alzerm in the Royal Laboratory.

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:29.360
I want to know everything there is about Delzaine.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:32.570
I have a responsibility to find out the truth about him.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:36.910
I can tell you everything
I know about King Delzaine.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:40.340
Allow me to help as well.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.740
Thank you.

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:47.580
I'll report back everything that happens in the north.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.580
Good. Please do.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.450
I heard you're the one who suggested some Ignauts come on our mission.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:55.120
You have my sincere gratitude.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.190
It's nothing...

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:58.090
Father!

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.700
When I grow up, I'm joining the Ignauts, too!

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:04.770
Then you and I can travel the world together!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.630
Not a bad idea!

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:10.040
You can be a future Ignaut starting today!

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:13.040
Thanks! Um...

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:15.440
I'm Shun. Shun Asanaga.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.710
And this is...

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.080
Emilio.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.580
Emilio Langheim.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.310
The son of King Delzaine.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.380
I see... It was you...

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.760
So Demetrio found it after all.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.230
What's that?

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:37.500
The light of hope for this country.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:43.840
It's still small right now, but soon it'll be a guiding beacon.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.980
I thought you abandoned your status.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:51.150
I had intended to.

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:57.280
But I'm done ignoring how much I hated him and the current plight of the country.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.750
I see...

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.890
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:13.770
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:23.270
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:46.030
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:56.030
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:05.220
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:13.830
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:22.370
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:31.540
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>
